message: "If you use this package, please cite it as below."
title: "AB-Cloud Research Programme: Unified Academic Package (spectral core, Dirac skeleton, Hilbert-Polya bridge, blind verification)"
authors:
  - family-names: "Isaev"
    given-names: "Iskhak Khamzatovich"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-7299-0701"
date-released: "2026-10-14"
repository-code: "https://github.com/wild8highlander/ab-cloud-research/tree/main/AB_Cloud_Academic_Package"
abstract: >-
  The unified academic edition of the AB-Cloud research programme: one study
  in four levels. The algebraic AB (Aharonov-Bohm) architecture as a computing
  fabric that reads mathematics in real time and stores nothing (campaigns
  V01-V20, theorems Th1-Th6, the V13 obligation machine keeping RH honestly
  blocked); its Dirac skeleton unpacked into a complete cross-verified
  lattice-Dirac identity (D1-D14: the pi-flux lattice is a discretized
  massless Dirac equation, the zeta-decorated operator lifts GOE to GUE);
  the Hilbert-Polya bridge with sixteen campaigns and eighteen theorems
  (the operator that almost exists - the wall is locality); and the blind
  verification apparatus (E01-E18: blind reading of all 649 zeta zeros up
  to T=1000 by two independent engines, bit-exact cross-engine agreement).
  Includes the unified monograph (full RU/EN volumes plus five language
  abstracts), the interactive web laboratory, the unified multi-language CLI
  (Python, Julia, Rust, Go, JS, Bash), curated datasets, and a complete
  honesty layer with does_not_prove fields on every claim.
keywords:
  - Riemann zeta
  - Hilbert-Polya
  - Aharonov-Bohm
  - lattice Dirac operator
  - random matrix theory
  - GUE
  - Berry-Keating
  - Connes
  - numerical verification
  - reproducibility
